  "description": "Discontinued, replaced by the current BFe, which has a full 29er wheel setup option. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic BFeMAX.\n\nThe BFeMAX was our radical, big wheel, rock smashing, hardcore hardtail. A crazy fast, super tough 29er, it was the result of gene-splicing our award winning SolarisMAX 29er trail hardtail with our tough-as-old-boots, 27.5\" wheeled BFe.\n\nIf you were looking for the fastest descending hardtail possible, this was it. With up to a 160mm fork and 29 inch wheels, the BFeMAX screamed come and have a go: jumps, drops, big mountains, hacking about in the woods and steamrollering down just about anything. There was room for meaty 2.6\" tyres with space for mud, and the big wheels carried momentum up and along, then let you grab the bike by the scruff of its neck on the way down. It kept the legendary toughness of the BFe, with a Reynolds 853 down tube spine and Cotic FM custom butted tubeset through the rest of the frame for the classic Cotic ride feel.\n\nFinishes: Smoke, Matte Fast Red, Bright Blue, Bright Blue and Magenta, Sunny Yellow, Gunmetal and Copper, and Dark Grey.\n\nI've done everything on this bike; there's nothing that it can't handle. You can do anything on it: jumps, downhill trails, XC rides and dual races. It's so easy to maintain, which as a mechanic is very important to me. The BFeMAX never missed a beat. It always made me feel like the fastest guy on the hill.\n\nWill Swinden, Cotic workshop mechanic, who raced his BFeMAX around the Peak District and rode it on some of the roughest trails in Scotland",
